## 2. Contract proposal and product behavior

All of this is proposed unless §10 marks it ruled.

### 2.1 Rule rendering (MG1)

`gnd.api.verbalize_rules(model, *, fact_types=None) -> dict`, schema
`gnd-rule-verbalization/1`. One entry per derived fact type, in stable id
order: `status` `rendered` with `text`, or `unsupported` with a list of
`{path, reason}`. Reasons: `prose-rule`, `unanalyzable-aggregate`,
`unrecognized-term`, `unrecognized-atom`. A rendered `text` equals the rule
sentence inside the full model verbalization. Exit 0 with some rules
unsupported; 3 for a bad model or unknown id; 64 for a malformed argument.
API only, no CLI leaf. Detail: [phase-MG1-spec.md](phase-MG1-spec.md).

### 2.2 Additive policy (MG2)

`gnd evolve preview --policy additive` (default: no policy, as today). The
policy refuses a proposal holding any of:

| Class | Operations |
|---|---|
| Change to existing structure | any `RENAME` or `DELETE`; any `MODIFY` of an object type, fact type or role that existed in the before-model |
| Reference scheme | a `MODIFY` changing an existing object type's `reference` (mode, value type, unit or composite) |
| Constraint on a populated fact type | an `ADD` of a constraint, or a `MODIFY` that strengthens one (MG-D3), on a fact type that is *populated* (MG-D4) |

Additions are allowed: new object types, new fact types, new roles only on new
fact types, new constraints on fact types that are not populated, and
description or provenance edits that change no structure (MG-D5).

The verdict is one function `additive_policy_issues(before, proposal, *,
populated) -> tuple[PolicyIssue, ...]` in `gnd.evolve`. Preview records the
policy name and its issues in the preview document (MG-D2) and exits 3 when
any issue exists, naming each refused operation by index and locator. `apply`
reads the policy from the preview, re-runs the function on the bytes it would
publish, and refuses on any issue (MG-R3).

### 2.3 Duplicate-shape report (MG3)

Preview gains a `shape_matches` list: for every `ADD` of a fact type, each
existing fact type whose **role-player signature** equals the new one's, with
its id and reading. The signature is the multiset of `(object type,
reference identity)` over roles, where reference identity comes from
`refscheme.reference_identity` and value types resolve to their primitive.
Role order does not matter, and supertypes do not match subtypes (MG-D7). The
report is advice (MG-R4): no exit or `breaking` change. Whether it enters the
preview digest is MG-D2.

### 2.4 Guideline artifact (MG4)

`gnd extract --guidelines` writes `<stem>.guidelines.md`, recorded with its
SHA-256 in `artifacts.json` (absent without the flag, so MG-R1 holds). For
each fact type: its readings; per role, the role name, the object type, the
object type's description core keys (`summary`, `row`, `source`, `notes`) and
its reference mode. Value constraints: see MG-D6. Constraint verbalization
stays out of `verbalization.txt`. The guideline generator is one function
in `extract/`, using MG3's signature helper for reference modes.

### 2.5 Unattended mode (MG5)

A model whose `source` object holds `mode: unattended` must also hold
`reviewer: none` and `documents: [{sha256, label}]`. Validation in this mode:

1. refuses any `status: confirmed` and any `source: user-supplied`;
2. requires a `provenance.spans` list on every object type, fact type and
   constraint whose source is `explicit`, `sample` or `llm-inferred`; each
   span is `{document_sha256, start, end, excerpt_sha256}` and names a
   declared document; `common-sense` constraints cite `library_entry` as
   today (MG-D8);
3. keeps the D-03 rule, so proposed `llm-inferred`, `sample` and
   `common-sense` constraints stay `deontic`.

`gnd validate --document PATH` (repeatable, optional) re-hashes spans against
supplied documents, as `bind_anchors` does for populations (MG-D9). Without
`mode: unattended`, nothing about validation changes. The skill gains an
Unattended mode distinct from One-shot, because One-shot auto-confirms
library-tier proposals (`SKILL.md:101,257`), which this mode forbids (MG-D10).

## 3. Dependencies and artifact homes

MG1, MG2, MG4 and MG5 are independent. MG3 follows MG2 because both change
the preview document and should take one versioned change (MG-D2). MG4 uses
MG3's signature helper; if MG4 runs first it creates the helper and MG3
reuses it. MG6 follows all five; its first checkpoint needs only the
approved plan. Close follows MG6. The successor milestone's CT4 needs MG2
and MG3 merged.

| Artifact | Home |
|---|---|
| Plan, specs, records, reviews | `.gnd-planning/milestones/model-growth-guardrails/` |
| Rule renderer | `src/gnd/model_verbalization.py`; wrapper in `src/gnd/api.py`; `src/gnd/rule-verbalization.schema.json` (MG1) |
| Additive policy | `src/gnd/evolve/policy.py` (new, lane `evolve`), called from `evolve/service.py` preview and apply; CLI in `commands/evolve.py` (MG2) |
| Role-player signature | `src/gnd/model_queries.py` or `model_index.py` (layer `model`; fixed in the MG3 or MG4 spec, whichever runs first) |
| Shape report | `src/gnd/evolve/service.py`, preview models in `evolve/models.py` (MG3) |
| Guideline generator | `src/gnd/extract/guidelines.py` (new, lane `extract`); CLI flag in `commands/extract.py`; `codegen/emit.py` mirror if MG-D11 says so (MG4) |
| Unattended validation | `src/gnd/model/_validation.py` (one rule), `orm-meta.schema.json` (`$defs.source_span`) (MG5) |
| Skill text | `src/gnd/skills/gnd-model-from-text/SKILL.md`, `gnd-orm-core/references/representation-format.md` (MG5; sync-pinned twins per AGENTS.md) |
| Docs | each phase's reference page; MG6 everything else |

## 4. Phases

### MG1: Public rule rendering (#72; about 110 source lines, 300 test lines)

Spec: [phase-MG1-spec.md](phase-MG1-spec.md), r1, awaiting review and owner
gate.

- **MG1-C1:** `verbalize_rules` and `render_rule_verbalizations` as §2.1; pins
  updated.
- **MG1-C2:** corpus parity: every rendered text equals its substring in the
  full verbalization, over every example and fixture model with a rule (61
  models, 116 rules measured at `1446f90`), with every construct present.
- **MG1-C3:** each reason reachable through validation has a case; each one
  that is not is shown unreachable by citing the validator rule (MG1-Q1).
- **MG1-C4:** evolve, recovery and RF1 suites unchanged.

### MG2: Additive policy on evolve (#75; about 200 source lines, 450 test lines)

- **MG2-C1:** one case per refused class in §2.2 that fails without the
  policy, and one per allowed class that the policy admits.
- **MG2-C2:** strengthening and populated as ruled in MG-D3 and MG-D4, each
  reading with a discriminating fixture.
- **MG2-C3:** the policy and its issues are in the digested preview; `apply`
  refuses a preview with issues; `apply` refuses a hand-edited preview that
  drops them; `apply` with a preview made without the policy is unchanged.
- **MG2-C4:** without `--policy`, every evolve golden and test is unchanged
  (MG-R1).

### MG3: Duplicate-shape report (#76; about 100 source lines, 250 test lines)

- **MG3-C1:** the signature helper, with cases for role order, repeated
  object types, value types resolved to primitives, composite reference
  schemes, and a subtype that does not match.
- **MG3-C2:** `shape_matches` in preview for every added fact type, stable
  order, with readings.
- **MG3-C3:** no exit, `breaking` or existing digest input changes (MG-R4).
- **MG3-C4:** a time-bound test: a model with 5,000 fact types and a proposal
  adding 500 matches in a counted linear number of signature reads.

### MG4: Extraction guidelines (#78; about 150 source lines, 300 test lines)

- **MG4-C1:** `--guidelines` writes the artifact and its digest; without the
  flag, bundles are byte-identical (MG-R1); `_artifact_index_issue`
  consumers accept the extra file; file-set pins updated only for the
  flag-on case.
- **MG4-C2:** `test_vocabulary_is_constraint_blind` still passes; a new test
  injects constraints into a model and shows the guideline changes only as
  MG-D6 allows.
- **MG4-C3:** the docs state that a description can restate a constraint, and
  that the guideline repeats descriptions verbatim (O20).

### MG5: Unattended model-from-text (#74; about 150 source lines, 400 test lines, skill text)

- **MG5-C1:** schema `$defs.source_span` and the `source` keys of §2.5,
  validated only when `mode: unattended`.
- **MG5-C2:** the validation rule's refusals, one case each, each failing
  without the rule; an unattended model with only `proposed` elements and
  complete spans exits 0.
- **MG5-C3:** `gnd validate --document` re-hash: a span whose excerpt digest
  differs exits 3; a document not declared in `source.documents` exits 3.
- **MG5-C4:** every packaged and fixture model validates exactly as before
  (MG-R1).
- **MG5-C5:** the skill's Unattended mode section and the representation
  reference, synced to their twins.

### MG6: Documentation

- **MG6-C1:** disposition table over every page and skill reference naming
  the API surface, evolve preview, the extract bundle or model-from-text
  modes.
- **MG6-C2:** checkpoint DC1 (illustrative drafts after plan approval,
  uncommitted) and DC2 (real runs after MG5), shown to the owner (O22).
- **MG6-C3:** one how-to: growing a model by additions with GND checking each
  round (preview with `--policy additive`, the shape report, extraction with
  guidelines, rule read-back). Registered with the docs runner and executed.
- **MG6-C4:** release notes; docs gates exit 0.
- **MG6-C5:** one independent docs reviewer against the shipped behaviour.

### Milestone close (not a feature phase)

Final parity, the close review (MG-D1), the question sweep, carryover O23 to
the reporter, and a PR.

