## 5. Documentation, skill and compatibility surfaces

- New: one `gnd.api` callable and its payload schema (MG1); one evolve option
  and preview fields (MG2, MG3); one extract option and artifact (MG4); one
  validate option, one schema `$def` and one skill mode (MG5).
- **Without the new options:** model verbalization, evolve previews and
  applies, extract bundles and validation are unchanged (MG-R1). Changes that
  cannot be avoided: `gnd.api.__all__` grows by one name; root help and RF1
  CLI goldens list the new options; the preview document schema changes if
  MG-D2 says so.
- Packaged skills: `gnd-model-from-text` (MG5), `gnd-model-evolve` (MG2, MG3
  mention the option and report), `gnd-extract` (MG4). Twins kept
  byte-identical.

## 6. Risks and required controls

| Risk | Control |
|---|---|
| A rule text change moves digest-bound verbalizations | MG-R1; MG1 adds a collector argument only; evolve and recovery suites unchanged |
| The additive policy is bypassed by editing the preview | MG-R3: `apply` re-runs the policy on its own bytes |
| "Strengthening" means different things to the caller and to GND | MG-D3 picks one closed list; docs state it; each item has a case |
| "Populated" is undecidable from preview's inputs | MG-D4 restricts it to what preview can read |
| The shape report is read as "these are duplicates" | MG-R4; field named `shape_matches`, docs say candidate |
| The guideline reintroduces constraint bias | MG-D6; MG4-C2 injection test |
| Unattended mode breaks existing models | Rule applies only when `mode: unattended`; MG5-C4 |
| One-shot and Unattended are confused | Distinct mode names; skill table contrasts them |
| Spans cite documents that do not exist | `source.documents` closed list; optional re-hash (MG5-C3) |
| Downstream names leak | MG-R7 |
| Repair rounds introduce defects | §8 stop rule |

## 7. Out of scope

- Composing populations and anchors across documents; proposing types from a
  population (successor milestone).
- Changing any rule's wording; a CLI for rule rendering.
- Semantic duplicate detection (synonym readings, embeddings); refusing on a
  shape match.
- Migrating facts between fact types; any evolve operation beyond the four
  kinds.
- Running `gnd-model-from-text` unattended inside GND (GND validates the
  result; the host runs the LLM).
- Publication, release, certification.

## 8. Execution, approval and review protocol

`auto=false`. Each phase follows `process-phase`: spec, owner gate,
implementation and focused tests, an independent diff review, a refactoring
review and a record. No code before recorded spec approval. Plan and close
review instrument: MG-D1. Stop rule (declared before round two, per
`review-convergence.md`): at most two plan review rounds; stop early when the
self-inflicted ratio exceeds one half. Work happens on a topic branch, then a
PR; merge requires the owner.

## 9. Per-phase verification story

| Phase | Expected result | Focused gate |
|---|---|---|
| MG1 | Corpus parity; reasons; pins | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_rule_verbalization.py tests/test_public_api.py tests/test_v61_phase2_api.py tests/test_public_runtime.py tests/test_why_not_near_misses_public.py tests/test_disclosure_mode.py tests/test_rf1_layering.py tests/test_rf6_query_policy.py tests/test_gnd_arch.py` plus the evolve and recovery test files (exact list fixed in the spec) |
| MG2 | Refusal per class; apply re-check; unset parity | evolve test files plus a new `tests/test_evolve_additive_policy.py`; RF1 CLI pins (unresolved until the spec) |
| MG3 | Signature cases; report; no gate change | MG2 gate plus `tests/test_evolve_shape_matches.py` |
| MG4 | Artifact and digest; flag-off parity; constraint injection | `tests/test_extract_*.py`, `tests/test_fidelity_stub_gate.py`, `tests/test_public_legacy_codegen_pins.py`, a new `tests/test_extract_guidelines.py` |
| MG5 | Refusals; re-hash; corpus parity | `tests/test_model_*.py` validation files (fixed in the spec), a new `tests/test_unattended_mode.py`, the skill twin sync test |
| MG6 | Pages executed; checkpoints seen | `tools/run_tutorials.py`, `zensical build --strict`, `tools/check_docs.py site` |

The broad suite runs on explicit owner selection.

## 10. Owner decisions and open questions

| ID | Question | Readings and cost | Proposal |
|---|---|---|---|
| MG-D1 | Plan and close review instrument | (a) four local readers, as the last two milestones; (b) six-seat panel: needs provider credentials, slower | **Ruled `(o1)`: (a)** for plan review; close review confirmed at the plan gate |
| MG-D2 | Preview document change for MG2 and MG3 | (a) one new preview schema version carrying `policy`, `policy_issues` and `shape_matches`, all inside the digest; (b) policy inside, shape report outside the digest: the report could be edited without detection, harmless because it is advice; (c) keep v3, put the policy in the proposal: `apply` then trusts proposal bytes | (a), with MG-R1 satisfied because a preview without the new options keeps the old version |
| MG-D3 | What counts as strengthening a constraint | (a) closed list: a new mandatory; a new or narrower uniqueness; a narrowed value set or range; a frequency `min` raised or `max` lowered; `deontic`→`alethic`; `proposed`→`confirmed` on an existing alethic constraint; (b) any `MODIFY` of a constraint on a populated fact type: simpler, refuses harmless edits (rationale text) | (a) |
| MG-D4 | What "populated" means | Preview reads no population contents. (a) a fact type with `sample_population` rows, owned by a reference population, or named by a supplied population artifact locator; (b) also accept `--populated FT` repeatable from the caller; (c) treat every existing fact type as populated: refuses any new constraint on an existing fact type | (a)+(b): the caller knows which types hold admitted facts |
| MG-D5 | Description and provenance edits on existing elements | (a) allowed: they change no structure; (b) refused as a `MODIFY` | (a) |
| MG-D6 | Value constraints in the guideline | The issue asks for them; the bundle is deliberately constraint-blind (`extract/vocabulary.py:3-17`, pinned). (a) omit value constraints; guideline holds readings, descriptions, reference modes, value-type primitives; (b) include them under a second flag `--guidelines-with-values`, marked as excluded from fidelity measurement; (c) include them by default: breaks the constraint-blind principle | (a), with (b) as an owner option |
| MG-D7 | Signature match rule | (a) role-order-free multiset, exact object types, primitives for value types, no supertype matching; (b) also match through supertypes: more matches, more noise | (a) |
| MG-D8 | Which elements need spans in unattended mode | (a) object types, fact types and constraints with source `explicit`, `sample` or `llm-inferred`; `common-sense` cites `library_entry`; (b) every element including common-sense: no span exists for library knowledge | (a) |
| MG-D9 | Span re-hash | (a) optional `gnd validate --document`; shape-only otherwise; (b) mandatory documents for unattended models: `gnd validate` would need the documents everywhere the model goes | (a) |
| MG-D10 | Skill mode | (a) a new Unattended mode, One-shot unchanged; (b) change One-shot to stop auto-confirming: changes current users' results | (a) |
| MG-D11 | Codegen bundle mirror | (a) codegen does not emit the guideline; (b) mirror it: more pins, no requested use | (a) |

